<%# Step two: which of the organization's repositories.

    locals: organization (a GithubOrganizations::Org)

    Every row here is a repository the SpecGuard GitHub App is installed on AND that GitHub lists
    this viewer as an administrator of. Nothing on this page is a gate: the tick boxes are
    client-controlled, so `BulkRegistration` re-asks GitHub about every submitted name before it
    saves anything. What the page is responsible for is not offering a click that can only fail —
    which is why already-registered rows are shown but not selectable, and why the connected
    repositories this viewer does not administer are counted rather than listed. %>
<% administered = organization.administered %>
<% registerable = administered.reject { |repo| already_registered?(repo.full_name) } %>
<% already = administered.length - registerable.length %>

<div class="space-y-4">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <%= render UI::HeadingComponent.new(level: 3, class: "text-app-content break-words") { organization.login } %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-app-content-secondary">
        <%# Each of these is composed as one string rather than assembled across ERB lines: a
            newline inside a sentence renders fine and is invisible to anything reading the text. %>
        <%= pluralize(administered.length, "repository", plural: "repositories") %> you administer.
        <% if already.positive? %>
          <%= "#{already == 1 ? 'One is' : "#{already} are"} already registered and cannot be registered again." %>
        <% end %>
        <%= withheld_repositories_sentence(organization.withheld_count) %>
      </p>
      <%# The carried batch came back SHORT — said here, beside the other "your list is short, here
          is why" sentence, because it is the same kind of fact and a reader scanning for one should
          find the other. A separate paragraph rather than another clause in the one above: that one
          describes the LISTING ("12 repositories you administer"), while this describes what
          happened to the READER'S SELECTION on a trip they just took, and it carries an action.

          Every argument here is evidence the helper needs to say only what is TRUE of each name,
          and none of them is optional — the helper's comment sets out the four states and why
          merging any two of them makes the page state a falsehood. In short:

            @full_names   what was carried. Read directly rather than passed in, because the
                          `github_full_names[]` checkbox below reads exactly that and the two must
                          be asking about one list. Same for the comparison — see the helper, which
                          mirrors `Array#include?` case-sensitively on purpose.
            administered  which carried names have NO ROW. Not `registerable`: an already-registered
                          name HAS a row (rendered below, disabled, with a badge saying so), which
                          is the page accounting for it.
            visible       what is CONNECTED, administered or not — the same set `withheld_count` is
                          derived from, four lines up. It separates "no row because it is not in
                          the installation" from "no row because you do not administer it", which
                          are different facts with different fixes, and which this paragraph would
                          otherwise report as one. Without it the page can say a repository is not
                          connected directly beneath a sentence saying one connected repository is
                          not listed — about the same repository.
            account       whose picker this is, so a carried name from another account is not
                          bucketed against a list that was never about it.
            registered    what is already IN SpecGuard, so it is not reported as a shortfall at
                          all — it is connected, and the reader's goal for it is already met.
                          Derived from `organization.repos` and not from `administered`, because
                          the exclusion has to cover the withheld bucket too: a repository
                          somebody else registered can be visible-but-not-administered here, and
                          telling this reader to "ask an administrator to register it" would be
                          asking for a thing already done. Same set `already_registered?` is
                          computed from four lines up, so it costs no read of its own.
            complete      whether ABSENCE is GitHub's answer or merely ours. The page-side reading
                          of the rule `name_verdict` enforces on the server; with the listing short,
                          the "not connected — add it on GitHub" claim is withheld rather than
                          guessed. Nothing else on this branch of `new.html.erb` says the listing is
                          incomplete, so this is the only thing standing between a truncated read
                          and a confident false sentence. %>
      <% shortfall = unmatched_carried_repositories_sentence(
           @full_names, administered.map(&:full_name),
           visible: organization.repos.map(&:full_name),
           account: organization.login,
           complete: github_listing_complete?,
           registered: organization.repos.map(&:full_name).select { |name| already_registered?(name) }
         ) %>
      <% if shortfall %>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-app-content-secondary"><%= shortfall %></p>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <%= render UI::ButtonComponent.new(variant: :ghost, size: :sm, href: bulk_repositories_path) do %>
      Change account
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <% if registerable.empty? %>
    <%# Everything this viewer administers here is already registered. That is a success, not an
        empty state to apologise for, so it says so and points at the list rather than at a form
        that could do nothing. %>
    <%= render UI::EmptyStateComponent.new(
          title: "Nothing left to register",
          description: "Every repository you administer in #{organization.login} is already " \
                       "registered in SpecGuard."
        ) do %>
      <%= render UI::ButtonComponent.new(variant: :primary, href: repositories_path) { "Back to repositories" } %>
    <% end %>
  <% else %>
    <%# `turbo: false` is what makes the summary reachable, and it is load-bearing rather than
        incidental. Turbo Drive REQUIRES a redirect in response to a form submission: a 200 with a
        rendered body is refused with "Form responses must redirect to another location", logged to
        the console and otherwise swallowed. `#create` answers with a rendered summary by design
        (see the controller's class comment for why a 20-row result is not flash material), so under
        Turbo the repositories would be registered and the user would see the picker sit there
        unchanged — silent success, the worst available failure for this action. Opting this one
        form out of Turbo keeps the render-don't-flash design and costs a full page load on a
        request that is already doing N GitHub verifications inline.

        Note the refusal paths are NOT why this is here: `render_refusal` returns 422 and Turbo
        renders 4xx happily. It is only the success path Turbo drops. %>
    <%= form_with url: bulk_repositories_path, method: :post,
                  data: { controller: "bulk-picker", turbo: false } do %>
      <%# Carried so a 422 re-render (nothing selected, too many selected) comes back to the same
          organization rather than dropping the reader at the chooser with their selection gone. %>
      <%= hidden_field_tag :organization, organization.login %>

      <div class="space-y-1">
        <%= label_tag :repository_query, "Search #{organization.login}",
                      class: "block text-sm font-medium text-app-content" %>
        <%= text_field_tag :repository_query, nil,
                           placeholder: "Start typing to narrow the list…",
                           autocomplete: "off",
                           data: { bulk_picker_target: "query",
                                   action: "input->bulk-picker#refine" },
                           class: Forms::FieldComponent::INPUT_CLASS %>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 border-b border-app-border-light pb-2">
        <%# Selects what is CURRENTLY SHOWN, not the whole organization — narrowing to "service"
            and pressing this is how a reader picks a subset of forty repositories, and a control
            that quietly reached past the narrowing would register things they had filtered out of
            view. With JavaScript off it is inert and the rows are ticked individually; nothing
            here is required to submit the form. %>
        <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-app-content">
          <%= check_box_tag :bulk_picker_all, "1", false,
                            id: "bulk-picker-all",
                            data: { bulk_picker_target: "all",
                                    action: "change->bulk-picker#chooseShown" },
                            class: "size-4 accent-app-cta" %>
          Select all shown
        </label>
        <p class="text-xs text-app-muted" data-bulk-picker-target="count"></p>
      </div>

      <ul class="mt-2 max-h-96 divide-y divide-app-border-light overflow-y-auto">
        <% administered.each_with_index do |repo, index| %>
          <% taken = already_registered?(repo.full_name) %>
          <li class="py-2"
              data-bulk-picker-target="row"
              data-bulk-picker-name="<%= repo.full_name.downcase %>">
            <label class="flex items-start gap-3 <%= taken ? "cursor-not-allowed opacity-60" : "cursor-pointer" %>"
                   for="bulk-pick-<%= index %>">
              <%= check_box_tag "github_full_names[]", repo.full_name,
                                !taken && @full_names.include?(repo.full_name),
                                id: "bulk-pick-#{index}",
                                disabled: taken,
                                data: { bulk_picker_target: "pick",
                                        action: "change->bulk-picker#tally" },
                                class: "mt-0.5 size-4 shrink-0 accent-app-cta" %>
              <span class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                <span class="block break-words text-sm text-app-content"><%= repo.full_name %></span>
                <span class="mt-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1">
                  <%# `private` and `archived` change what registering the repository will MEAN — an
                      archived one will never push another CI run — so they are on the row rather
                      than discoverable afterwards. Same two facts the single-repository picker puts
                      on its option label. %>
                  <% if taken %>
                    <%= render UI::BadgeComponent.new(tone: :info) { "Already registered" } %>
                  <% end %>
                  <% if repo.private? %>
                    <%= render UI::BadgeComponent.new(tone: :neutral) { "private" } %>
                  <% end %>
                  <% if repo.archived? %>
                    <%= render UI::BadgeComponent.new(tone: :warning) { "archived" } %>
                  <% end %>
                </span>
              </span>
            </label>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>

      <%# The batch bound, stated only when this organization can actually reach it. A limit a
          reader cannot hit is noise; one they can is something to know before they tick forty
          boxes and have the submission refused. %>
      <% if registerable.length > BulkRegistration::MAX_BATCH %>
        <%= render UI::AlertComponent.new(tone: :warning, class: "mt-3") do %>
          At most <%= BulkRegistration::MAX_BATCH %> repositories can be registered in one batch.
          Register the rest in a second pass.
        <% end %>
      <% end %>

      <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <%= render UI::ButtonComponent.new(variant: :primary, type: "submit") { "Register selected repositories" } %>
        <%= render UI::ButtonComponent.new(variant: :ghost, href: repositories_path) { "Cancel" } %>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</div>
